#!RuleTest
#test DRAFT-900045 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "The sister half of the DRAFT-900043 gate (minted 2026-09-11, M17/T1-31 -- a copy of CDISC-CG0535 into the draft package, the only package the parent ships into). The DSSCAT column is absent (None satisfied) while subject 001 has two DISPOSITION EVENT records in the TREATMENT epoch, so the remaining condition holds on both rows; Sensitivity is Dataset, so the absence is reported ONCE, where the pre-gate parent flooded one finding per duplicated row. Same dataset shape as the parent's skipped_no_dsscat_column scenario: the parent skips, this rule reports."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT    type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col EPOCH    type=Char label="Epoch"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT | TREATMENT
S1 | DS | 001 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT | TREATMENT
